<!--
    Adaptive icon foreground: a white ring enclosing the rupee sign.

    The glyph is the real U+20B9 outline lifted from Arial Bold rather than drawn by hand -
    earlier hand-built versions came out as a franc sign, because the defining difference is
    subtle and easy to get wrong. Extracted with fontTools, scaled to 34dp tall and centred.

    Adaptive icons are 108x108dp but only the central 72x72dp is guaranteed visible; the outer
    18dp can be cropped by the launcher mask. Everything here stays within radius 34 of the
    centre, so the ring survives a circular mask as well as a squircle.

    Doubles as the monochrome layer for Android 13+ themed icons, where the system re-tints it.
-->
